2026-09-27T10:19:15.0816061Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0816257Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0816551Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0816820Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0816916Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0817499Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0817666Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0817817Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0818174Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0818392Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0818500Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0818765Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0818931Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0819059Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0819449Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0819792Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0820429Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0820937Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0821031Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0821437Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0821951Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0822219Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0822564Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0822953Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0823031Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0823224Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0823343Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0824564Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0825873Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0826080Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0826530Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0827603Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0828254Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0828811Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0901097Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0903951Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0904186Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0904682Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0904995Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0906780Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0908960Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0910074Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0911588Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:15.0911980Z 
